<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khababash</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 338–336 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khababash was an Egyptian ruler who led a revolt against Persian rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a> in the late 330s BCE, probably during the turmoil that followed the murders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxerxes-iii">Artaxerxes III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxerxes-iv">Artaxerxes IV</a>. He is known from a few documents, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">Satrap</a> Stela of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I</a>, which records a land grant he made to the gods of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buto">Buto</a>. Persian control was restored under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a> before Alexander's arrival.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khababash.jpg" alt="Khababash" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Richard Lepsius (1810-84) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stela_Nastasen_Kambasuten_Lepsius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
